	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00101" index="101">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00102" index="102">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00103" index="103">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00104" index="104">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00105" index="105">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00106" index="106">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: Ah - you must be the two\nfrom Cherrygrove.\rGold rang ahead about you.\rSaid a pair of his neighbors had\nfinally caught the bug.\rHe was right to send you. A Trainer\nwithout a Pokédex is a Trainer walking\fwith their eyes closed.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00107" index="107">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: Here. One for each of\nyou.\rIt records every Pokémon you meet and\nevery Pokémon you catch.\rThe more pages you fill, the more of\nthis world you’ll understand.\fThat’s the whole idea of it.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00108" index="108">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">{STRVAR_1 3, 0, 0} received the Pokédex\nfrom Professor Elm!\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00109" index="109">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: Check it whenever you\nsee a Pokémon you don’t know.\rIt fills its own pages. All you have\nto do is go and look.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00110" index="110">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: You know, the two of\nyou remind me of someone.\rTwo more, actually.\rGold started out from a town\njust like yours.\rWalked into this lab not much older\nthan you are now.\rAnd the other one... well. You know him\nas the Champion.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00111" index="111">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: Silver was a difficult\nboy back then. Sharp edges.\rA chip on his shoulder the size of\nMt. Silver.\rBut people change.\rHe turned all that fire into something\nthe whole world could lean on.\rChampion. Protector. Proof that no one\nis only the worst day of their life.\fI’ve never been prouder of two\nstudents.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00112" index="112">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Professor Elm: Go on, then. Your\nroad’s waiting.\rAnd do an old professor a favor -\nfill those pages.\r</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0543_T20R0101_00113" index="113">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">KESTRA: Did you hear that? The\nChampion started right here.\rSame lab. Same professor. Same dinky\nlittle Pokédex.\rThat’s gonna be us. I can feel it.\fCome on - let’s go tell Gold we’re\nofficially Trainers!\r</language>
	</row>
</body>
